{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:f23a3ecdb051b4e473af77f0aa82b01ceb725a3f0e6b0880063df3a3bde1c660","title":"How does a gauge theory separate from gravity when an ADE singularity develops inside a compact K3-fibered Calabi–Yau threefold?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f292ba4fe90e4db888614090872cee2ecbd160b22db7bf4796412bee4350c903","title":"Can a gauge-invariant non-Abelian field drive homogeneous, isotropic slow-roll inflation, and can a two-parameter realization produce perturbation spectra compatible with the cosmological data available to the authors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2f7b77b133d2dda8c66424463970c02120cc97a43e897f8fc4dc6a2a1b7889d","title":"How should observables, horizon entropy and quantum gravity be formulated in asymptotically de Sitter space, distinguishing a static-patch observer from a metaobserver accessing future-boundary data?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2107ba4391515831703f47d5d2f16773f60be9737f4c55764ce5ceeb6fd5603","title":"How do field mass and charge affect Kerr–Newman scalar quasinormal modes, exterior stability, late-time tails and near-extremal mode branching beyond small μM and qQ?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f208201c60b72fdd70b35c7d69c3fedc571c52d157cc73bfad2b7e23b0636649","title":"Can KNP alignment of the universal RR axion C0 and one orientifold-odd C2 axion produce a trans-Planckian effective decay constant in weakly coupled type IIB large-volume compactifications while retaining moduli stabilization?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2a4cd6c6db7f6636d11cdb603d3b623ade964b12e888c7a9ad169e7e2edd3bd","title":"How does anomalous gravitational dressing of the cosmological-constant operator modify semiclassical gravitational dynamics near two dimensions, and can its cosmological consequences suggest mechanisms for vacuum-energy decay, inflation and dark energy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0020"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f292ebe81993cf3529f2453014d183a3a9d346d7c643bbe49315840f921c2968","title":"Can a perturbatively massless 2-form have parametrically small coupling f without light charged strings or a low cutoff? The paper seeks a physical obstruction from axionic black-hole evaporation rather than assumptions about extremal black strings or gravitational instantons.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f285074aa73e823cd4197ab6a7bf821eac3771117b3054bafa3e563e2985becb","title":"Does de Sitter space remain self-consistent under semiclassical back reaction when the gravitational source is calculated after tracing over states beyond a local observer’s cosmological event horizon?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0024"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2183f1fb3b8458232f97b37db3de53d0804ba5ff542301adcad106fc3e2add0","title":"What corrections to the three-dimensional Kähler potential, complex coordinate and no-scale condition follow from reducing available eleven-dimensional eight-derivative terms on a one-Kähler-modulus Calabi–Yau fourfold, and how robust are they against additional G²R³ couplings?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f24263baf7890aa1019b1a3817d69b425cc1cf102f9b3fffe6e4dd5ba43b0b65","title":"Does eliminating ghost poles and improving ultraviolet behavior suffice for a higher-derivative theory to define a unitary fundamental quantum field theory? The paper tests this using Euclidean reflection positivity and spectral representations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f24433575f0e57886dd978afa51e96288c4849b8a4230ba0211bde49b3a5fbc1","title":"Are the assumed light scalar backgrounds stable against the same tower loops used to estimate their kinetic terms? The answer depends on potential protection, including supersymmetric pairing and the size of splittings within the relevant tower.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2cdeafa683543af33276f3f99efe6f636b151d9e670df6a6f8786a694e99376","title":"Does consistent quantum gravity forbid positive-energy de Sitter vacua or sustained potential slow roll? The paper investigates this question through restricted tree-level string compactifications while recognizing that their evidential scope is narrower than a universal quantum-gravity principle.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f248474915c717e6122e6f37fe1774ac5d988ec8889d78340311ad0dda1c9cec","title":"How does decompactification make KK states light when particle masses and the lower-dimensional Planck scale depend on the frame used to compare radii?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f234b2222c1c27bc7f486397c134eee201c7396fed98f731098d8b431ad9af25","title":"Which more general modified-gravity models can explain late-time acceleration while satisfying observational bounds and the assumed swampland conditions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2cdff49fd7ec50dfbce13851de62e9733e050cec225ae517e2bd849fd428e8f","title":"Under what conditions can two scalar fields realize constant-roll inflation, and does the resulting freedom in the potential improve prospects for matching string-inspired models compared with the rigid single-field construction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2797461a3ba84f3a7133c2c955ff3269b92b628731eb67b3143c90b7d6c722e","title":"Can relaxing an effective flux-quantization assumption give a hierarchical compactification a consistent finite field range? The paper tests this by relating heavy-field freezing diagnostics to two non-geometric flux parameters.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2f9610cdbb3fff9454a5035e9a17c24afbc2a18a5b3e91d2755de4e4532ce1a","title":"Can two gravitational backgrounds be joined locally at finite energy, even when their relation by duality requires compactification and an infinite-distance limit?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f292ab0dcc1705ec766ea8e97e3f4cb614ca8f3332f6da09002666ca9e7dc5da","title":"Can an axion coupled to electroweak SU(2) provide a sufficiently flat, sufficiently small dark-energy potential while satisfying the weak gravity conjecture, and can a supersymmetric extension resolve the apparent decay-constant tension?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f249e55f7ab78024a1d09ea0f63b416fd50ef53f9c14d2016a4f746dd9a09446","title":"Can multiple inflationary stages obey the trans-Planckian censorship conjecture while allowing high-scale observable inflation, preparing its initial smooth patch, explaining the present horizon, and accommodating eternal inflation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2bdf179119d3e3bdd7c8cb202788abefa20a2d32cdf2c12f3ae023b53258f15","title":"How can primordial tensor interactions be parameterized without choosing one inflaton Lagrangian? The source uses independent coefficients in an operator expansion around an inflationary clock background.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2b59ee9884ca68f2a95480498595abcd6aed5042649de410ef959100b3383f0","title":"Can a conjectured restriction on the total scalar potential constrain quark masses and the QCD angle through composite pion vacua? The paper also asks whether quintessence removes this proposed connection between quantum gravity and flavor.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2901a9f0b61c7ecdc2c591114511dcd6f446e015f794918f101cbb04c5f6e87","title":"Which derivative-interaction models remain worth testing after gravitational-wave, local-gravity and ISW restrictions? The paper selects a cubic potential-dominated scenario while distinguishing it from constrained tracker histories and noting possible loss of radiative protection.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f2b142dfe014c15ad04af0e33c6956a4852bd6b8ffeb70f54b07e4bbb6b7b5ea","title":"Which physical scale bounds a four-dimensional EFT obtained by compactifying string theory? The internal volume separates the KK threshold from the higher string scale, so the four-dimensional matching problem begins at the effective KK scale.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f24bd6e562f61f44e0a0e